.py`**: removed `_resolve_plugin_name` and the `inspect` import. Added `_function_path`, which unwraps `functools.partial` and uses `type(func).__call__` for callable instances. `BackgroundTask` now takes `(name, func)` and sets `.function` instead of `.plugin`. Added a read-only `launched` property on the supervisor.\n- **`datasette/app.py`**: added `_tasks()` next to `_threads`, with the five keys and no `plugin` key. Added the `/-/tasks(\\.json)?` route right after `/-/threads`, gated by `permissions-debug`. Updated the `add_background_task` docstring to name `.function`.\n- **`docs/introspection.rst`**: new `/-/tasks` section after `/-/threads`, with the permission requirement and an example JSON response.\n- **`docs/internals.rst`**: `.plugin` replaced by `.function` in the handle's attribute list.\n\n**Not done**\n- I did not commit. I did not edit the three test files, `docs/changelog.rst`, or anything else out of scope.\n- I ran only the spec's acceptance command, not the full test suite.\n\n**Unverified**\n- The three XPASS results come from an `xfail` on the `/fixtures/two` padlock test in `tests/test_permissions.py`. It's unrelated to background tasks, but I did not confirm it also XPASSes on the unmodified code.", "ttft_ms": 2494, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 57768, "uuid": "ac0af286-4651-4968-9f48-ec8b768c808b", "ttft_stream_ms": 2432, "time_to_request_ms": 803, "first_content_frame_ms": 2432, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
